[COMMENTS]
STATION,Crump weir gauging a gw influenced, rural catchment with Chalk bedrock overlain with superficial deposits and with only minor artificial influences, station is bypassed at high flows. GENERAL: Compound Crump weir with three sections - central low flow crest 0.6m, flanked by two crests 1.2m wide each. STATION HYDROMETRY: Bypasses at 2.3 cumecs. Can be affected by mill operations c 50m u/s. One rating applied across period of record. FLOW RECORD: Low flows in summer 2005 and 2008 affected by u/s mill operation. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9). FLOW REGIME: Gw-influenced regime, annual hydrographs reflect high baseflow component from the Chalk aquifer. Industrial/agricultural abstraction reduces natural runoff but impacts are minimal. Effluent returns increase runoff and may produce a minor net import from outside the catchment.
CATCHMENT,Predominantly Boulder Clay with some sand and gravel, underlying Chalk exposed in the valleys. Rural, predominantly arable.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Good fit to rating.
Pooling Suitability,AMAX3 is contained and flow is modular.
[END]
